#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1086 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "NEW with the M2-P2 ruling (option (a), Fix #303) - the per-family pin of the truncated-time class. PMDA-SD1086 is one of four byte-identical carriers of the CG0006 Check, and every one of the family's authority rows says 'date portion'; the four moved together so the group does not acquire a divergence it did not have. LBDTC '2020-01-15T09' is 13 characters - a complete date with a truncated time - which is_complete_date rejected (it gates on length 10/16/19) and is_complete_date_part accepts. The dy operation already computed 15 from the first ten characters, so the Check was discarding a correct answer; LBDY=14 now fires. Row 2 is the same shape with the correct day and stays silent."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=001
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test Short Name"
col LBDTC    type=Char label="Date/Time of Specimen Collection"
col LBDY     type=Num  label="Study Day of Specimen Collection"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | ALB | 2020-01-15T09 | 14
S1 | LB | 001 | 2 | ALB | 2020-01-10T09 | 10
---

dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFSTDTC type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
---
S1 | DM | 001 | 2020-01-01
---
